<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Great Game</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Great Game</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Game was the nineteenth-century rivalry between the British and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empires</a> for influence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. Russian expansion towards Afghanistan brought the two empires close, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> served as a buffer between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> and the Afghan frontier. It was eased by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-russian-convention">Anglo-Russian Convention</a> of 1907.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/the-great-game.jpg" alt="The Great Game" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edward Stanford Ltd. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stanfords_Map_of_Western_Asia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
